First, let's find an expression for $\dfrac{d}{dx}[2f(x)+2h(x)-3]$ in terms of $f'$ and $h'$:

$\begin{align}
&\phantom{=}\dfrac{d}{dx}[2f(x)+2h(x)-3]
\\\\
&=\dfrac{d}{dx}[2f(x)]+\dfrac{d}{dx}[2h(x)]-\dfrac{d}{dx}(3)&&\gray{\text{Sum and difference rules}}
\\\\
&=2f'(x)+2h'(x)-0&&\gray{\text{Constant and constant multiple rules}}
\end{align}$

So we found that $\dfrac{d}{dx}[2f(x)+2h(x)-3]=2f'(x)+2h'(x)$.
